<v Speaker 2>In the case of parents, Allah says in Surah Al-Luqman, Wa wassainal insana bi walidaihi hamalat hu ummuh wahnan 'ala wahnin wa fisaluhu fi 'aamain anishkurli wali walidaih ilayal masir.

62
00:08:23.470 --> 00:08:30.350
<v Speaker 2>And we have made it compulsory, we have enjoined upon human beings the care for their parents.

63
00:08:30.750 --> 00:08:32.110
<v Speaker 2>His mother carried him

64
00:08:32.910 --> 00:08:57.150
<v Speaker 2>increasing in weakness upon weakness and then in his weaning which is in two years so be grateful to me and to your parents because to me is the final destination so be grateful to me and both of your parents but then he says

65
00:09:02.150 --> 00:09:30.830
<v Speaker 2>but if your parents are working against you in forcing you to disbelieve and commit shirk against me then do not obey them but you still have to be what you still have to be grateful to them in other words if your parents are forcing you to disbelieve in Allah you don't have to praise them but you still have to be grateful to them

66
00:09:31.870 --> 00:09:34.910
